######################################################################
## Arweave 2.9.5.1 vm.args.src -- CONTAINER-TUNED.
##
## This is upstream's releases/2.9.5.1/vm.args.src verbatim, with ONE
## change: the three +sbwt* busy-wait thresholds are set to `none`.
##
## Upstream ships them as `very_long` and carries this hint, commented
## out, at line 28 of its own file:
##
##     ## Uncomment the following line if running in a container.
##     ## +sbwt none
##
## We are taking upstream's own advice. `very_long` makes the Erlang
## schedulers spin on CPU while waiting for work, which on a cgroup-
## limited container reads as ~100% CPU at idle, blows through the CPU
## request, and gets the pod CFS-throttled during real work.
##
## NOTHING ELSE IS CHANGED. The +MB* binary allocator tuning is
## load-bearing for Arweave's 100 MiB recall-range binaries -- do not
## "simplify" it.
##
## WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL:
##   bin/arweave regenerates releases/2.9.5.1/vm.args from this .src on
##   EVERY invocation (including `stop`, `ping`, `status`). That is a
##   write into the release directory. We redirect it with
##   RELX_OUT_FILE_PATH=/run/arweave so the image can stay read-only and
##   run as non-root. See the Dockerfile and 04-statefulset.yaml.
##
## Upstream source (tag N.2.9.5.1): config/vm.args.src
######################################################################

## Name of the node.
## Erlang distribution is bound to loopback only -- sys.config pins
## {kernel, [{inet_dist_use_interface, {127,0,0,1}}]} and epmd binds
## 127.0.0.1/::1. Nothing here is reachable from outside the pod, which
## is why the default cookie is acceptable for a single-pod StatefulSet.
## Override with the ARNODE / ARCOOKIE env vars if you ever cluster.
-name ${ARNODE:-arweave@127.0.0.1}

## Cookie for distributed erlang
-setcookie ${ARCOOKIE:-arweave}

## Disable the emulator break handler. Note this also makes the VM
## IGNORE SIGINT and SIGQUIT -- inside the pod only SIGTERM will stop
## the node. SIGTERM is still handled gracefully by OTP's
## erl_signal_handler -> init:stop() -> ar:prep_stop/1.
+Bi

## Enables the kernel poll functionality.
+Ktrue

## +A1024: emulator number of threads in the Async long thread pool for linked
## in drivers, mostly unused
+A1024

## +SDio1024: emulator Scheduler thread count for Dirty I/O, 200
## threads for file access
##
## NOTE: +A1024 and +SDio1024 together create ~2048 OS threads. That is
## sized for a many-partition miner. If the pod hits a pids limit, or
## you are on a 2-vCPU node, drop both to 128. See RUNBOOK section 11.
+SDio1024

## +MBsbct 103424: binary_alloc singleblock carrier threshold (in KiB)
## (101MiB, default 512KiB). Blocks larger than the threshold are
## placed in singleblock carriers. However multi-block carriers are
## more efficient. Since we have so many 100MiB binary blocks due to
## the recall range, set the threshold so that they are all placed in
## multi-block carriers and not single-block carriers.
+MBsbct 103424

## +MBsmbcs 10240: binary_alloc smallest multi-block carrier size (in
## KiB) (10MiB, default 256KiB).
+MBsmbcs 10240

## MBlmbcs 410629: binary_alloc largest multi-block carrier size (in
## KiB) (~401MiB, default 5MiB). Set so that a single multi-block
## carrier can hold roughly 4 full recall ranges.
##
## This is why the pod's memory limit must be generous -- a single
## allocator carrier here is ~401 MiB.
+MBlmbcs 410629

## +MBmmsbc 1024: binary_alloc maximum mseg_alloc singleblock carriers
## (1024 carriers, default 256). Once exhausted, the emulator will start
## using sys_alloc rather than mseg_alloc for singleblock carriers.
## This can be slower.
+MBmmmbc 1024

## +MBas aobf: emulator Memory Binary Allocation Strategy set to Address
## Order Best Fit.
## see: https://www.erlang.org/doc/man/erts_alloc.html#strategy
+MBas aobf

## ---- CHANGED FOR CONTAINERS (upstream ships `very_long` on all 3) ----
## Sets scheduler busy wait threshold.
+sbwt none

## Sets dirty scheduler busy wait threshold.
+sbwtdcpu none

## Sets dirty IO scheduler busy wait threshold
+sbwtdio none
## ---------------------------------------------------------------------

##  Sets scheduler wakeup threshold.
+swt very_low

##  Sets dirty scheduler wakeup threshold.
+swtdcpu very_low

## Sets dirty IO scheduler wakeup threshold.
+swtdio very_low
